              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Acepromazine 0.01–0.2 mg/kg IV/IM as needed to control paradoxical reactions.",
              "pdf_page": 252,
              "printed_page": 170,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cyproheptadine 1.1 mg/kg PO q4–6h or rectally for dogs; 2–4 mg/cat q4–6h for control of paradoxical reactions.",
              "pdf_page": 252,
              "printed_page": 170,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Flumazenil—a benzodiazepine reversal agent: 0.01 mg/kg IV q1–2h as needed; it can be used to reverse both excessive sedation and paradoxical reaction; however, flumazenil can cause seizures, so its use is generally restricted to life-threatening situations.",
              "pdf_page": 252,
              "printed_page": 170,
              "column": 1
            }
